/* IfcSheet test fixture for the structural grid (issue 47). Generated by a throw-away script, then read by hand.
   Units: MILLIMETRE, so a missing unit scale shows as a factor of 1000.
   Grid: axes A (x = 0), B (x = 6000) running along y, 1 (y = 0), 2 (y = 5000) running along x, in the grid's own frame.
   The storey's ObjectPlacement is relative to the IfcBuilding: translated (5000, -2000), elevation 3000 (Elevation
   attribute 3000 too). The grid's ObjectPlacement and the columns' and walls' are relative to the storey, as exports
   write them: the grid at (10000, 20000) rotated 15 degrees about Z; columns A1 B1 A2 B2 (400 x 400, 3000 high) and
   four walls on the grid lines at (10000,20000) + R(15deg) * (0|6000, 0|5000). Each axis passes through the centres
   of two columns, and only the storey step puts the grid where the meshes are (world offset (5000,-2000,3000)). FZK-Haus has no IfcGrid, hence this file. */
